From c31a66ab96ee942821f56442730142ac74531c5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:39:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] qualcommbe: add JioRouter AX6000 JIDU6J11
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add support for the JioRouter AX6000 (JIDU6J11 series), based on the
Qualcomm IPQ9554 SoC.

Supported variants: JIDU6111, JIDU6411, JIDU6611, JIDU6711, JIDU6811
and JIDU6911.

All variants share one dtsi. Each has its own dts that sets the model,
compatible and the ath11k calibration variant (JIDU<sku>, for example
JIDU6111) used to select the board data. The variants differ in board
data and in UART voltage (see below).

| Component        | Details                                           |
|------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| **SoC**          | Qualcomm IPQ9554 (4× ARM Cortex-A73 @ 1.5 GHz)    |
| **RAM**          | 512 MB DDR4                                       |
| **Flash**        | 256 MB SPI NAND                                   |
| **Ethernet**     | 5× Gigabit Ethernet (1 WAN + 4 LAN, QCA8075)      |
| **WLAN 2.4 GHz** | Integrated IPQ95XX AHB — 802.11b/g/n/ax, 4×4 MIMO |
| **WLAN 5 GHz**   | Qualcomm QCN9074 PCIe — 802.11a/n/ac/ax, 4×4 MIMO |
| **USB**          | 1× USB 3.0                                        |
| **LEDs**         | 3× GPIO-controlled (Red, Green, Blue)             |
| **Button**       | 1× Reset                                          |
| **UART**         | 115200 8N1, see voltage table below               |

**UART voltage:**

| Variant                  | UART level |
|--------------------------|------------|
| 6111, 6411, 6611         | 3.3 V      |
| 6711, 6811, 6911         | 1.8 V      |

**MAC Addresses:**

| Interface        | Source                     |
|------------------|----------------------------|
| WAN/Label        | ART partition, offset 0x00 |
| LAN (all ports)  | WAN + 1                    |
| 2.4 GHz          | WAN + 2                    |
| 5 GHz            | WAN + 3                    |

**Installation (TFTP + initramfs):**

Replace <sku> with your model's variant name: jidu6111, jidu6411,
jidu6611, jidu6711, jidu6811 or jidu6911.

Before flashing, back up the stock 0:ART, MFG and 0:BDF partitions
and save the output of U-Boot's printenv. The first sysupgrade
overwrites the boot environment, and ART holds the MAC addresses and
calibration data.

1. Connect to the UART console at 115200 baud, using an adapter set
   to the voltage listed above for your variant.
2. Set up a TFTP server and interrupt U-Boot autoboot.
3. Boot the initramfs image:

   ```sh
   setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1
   setenv serverip 192.168.1.2
   tftpboot 0x44000000 openwrt-qualcommbe-ipq95xx-jiorouter_ax6000-<sku>-initramfs-uImage.itb
   bootm 0x44000000
   ```

4. Transfer the sysupgrade image to `/tmp` and flash:

   ```sh
   sysupgrade /tmp/openwrt-qualcommbe-ipq95xx-jiorouter_ax6000-<sku>-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin
   ```

The first sysupgrade initializes the U-Boot environment (mtdparts,
bootcmd and bootargs) and configures NAND boot. Reverting
to stock requires restoring the saved values.

Signed-off-by: Sahil Bakshi <sahilbakshi2001@gmail.com>
